        "english_translation": "I moved into a new house last month. The rubbish days in this town are really tough. Monday is the day for food rubbish. On Tuesday you put out old clothes and shoes and the like. On Thursday you must not put out any rubbish other than paper. The paper with the rubbish days on it is long, and it is stuck up in front of the door. For the first week, every morning I read that paper and then looked at the rubbish bin. Sometimes I held the rubbish and stood in front of that paper for about an hour. Now I remember all of it. And so people nearby come every morning and ask, \"What rubbish is it today?\" The old lady stands in front of the door holding her rubbish bin, waiting. I still do not know the names of the people in town. But everyone calls me \"the rubbish person.\"",
