        "english_translation": "Last night a strong typhoon came to my town. Because of that, the trains have stopped today, and there are no classes at school either. Even so, the bread shop near the station opened its door at seven, the same time as always. Outside it was rain and wind, and there was a lot of water on the road. Wet customers come into the shop and buy bread. An old man bought two big loaves. A little girl holds her wet hat and stands behind her mother. Inside the shop it was warm, and the bread was hot. I also bought bread for breakfast and said \"Thank you\" to the shop clerk. The clerk said, \"That was a hard night, wasn't it?\" and gave me some tea.",
