        "english_translation": "On a summer night, I went alone to see the fireworks. But there were lots of big men in front, and I could not see the fireworks at all. So I climbed a small hill nearby. The top of the hill was dark, and there was no one there. I sat on a box and looked at the sky. Then a man in a black hat came and said, \"This is the place where the fireworks go up.\" And he said, \"That box is the fireworks. Please do not sit on it.\" I got off the box right away. The man looked at his watch and said, \"It will start soon. You may watch from here.\" I watched the fireworks from the best seat on the hill. They were very close, and the whole sky turned red. And my ears hurt for three days.",
